  "prompt": "Which months had more than 30,000 orders? Use the sales table, which has one row per order line, so one order can appear on several rows: count each order_id once. Its order_month column holds the first day of the month the order was placed in. Return two columns, in this order: order_month and n_orders, the number of different orders. Return one row per month, and only the months with more than 30,000 orders, sorted by order_month from earliest to latest.",
